{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe runner attaches per-call usage to every result (`result[\"_usage\"]`, src/rebar/llm/runner.py:543) but Pass-1 discards it: passes.pass1_chunk, passes.pass1_container, and passes.pass1_isf return findings lists only, so BatchRunResult.outputs (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:167-176) carries no usage key and plan-review coverage.metrics has call counts but no token totals for the most expensive pass (the gap is documented at src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-149; _attach_plan_review_metrics currently reconstructs only det_ms/llm_ms/llm_calls timing proxies). Per-criterion request counts are extracted (runner.py:_extract_usage) but never persisted, blocking data-driven criterion demotion decisions.\n\n## Approach\nrun_pass1 does not call runner.run directly — calls flow through _chunk -> sizing.pass1_with_ladder -> passes.pass1_chunk (and the container/ISF variants). The usage is threaded through that chain as a coordinated internal-API change, all callers updated atomically in this one change (these functions are private to the plan_review package; no external consumers): (1) passes.pass1_chunk, passes.pass1_container, and passes.pass1_isf change return type from list[dict] to (list[dict], dict) — findings plus the call's _usage dict; their complete caller set, each updated here: sizing.pass1_with_ladder (chunk path), pass1._chunk, pass1's container fan-out (_timed_pairing path), and pass1's ISF invocation. (2) Aggregation protocol: usage is recorded per CALL as {criteria: [ids the call covered], llm_calls, requests, input_tokens, output_tokens, cache_read_tokens, cache_write_tokens}. Ladder retries: every attempt pass1_with_ladder makes for a chunk — including escalation retries after a context-limit error — appends its own call record (billed is billed; retry usage is never discarded), all carrying the same criteria list. run_pass1 derives (a) the aggregate sum over all call records and (b) a per-criterion map using this attribution rule: an AGENT call (single criterion) attributes wholly to that criterion; a multi-criterion single-turn chunk attributes its token fields divided equally across its covered criteria (a documented approximation — the sidecar retains the raw per-call records, so exact attribution is always reconstructable), while llm_calls/requests count in full for each covered criterion. (3) The prerequisite finder runs in ProductionBatchRunner.run() via prerequisites.run_focused_finder, which returns (records, findings) with no usage — it is extended to return (records, findings, usage), its callers updated in the same change (scope includes src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py), and that usage is merged into the aggregate before emitting BatchRunResult.outputs[\"_usage\"]. (4) _attach_plan_review_metrics (src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py:249+) is EXTENDED to fold the new token totals from the batch step output into coverage.metrics alongside its existing timing fields. (5) The sidecar payload (src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py build_payload) gains coverage.usage = {\"per_call\": [call records], \"per_criterion\": {id: map}} — these exact key names are what the tests assert. Alternative rejected: post-hoc parsing of the REBAR_USAGE_LOG JSONL — opt-in, not always present, and not keyed by criterion.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/llm/plan_review/passes.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sizing.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/prerequisites.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/sidecar.py, src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py, tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py (new, beside tests/unit/workflow/test_production_batch_runner.py).\n\n## Testing\nUnit with FakeRunner emitting stub _usage dicts: aggregate totals equal the sum over chunk, agent, container, ISF, and prerequisite call records; a two-criterion chunk with 100 input tokens attributes 50 to each criterion while counting one llm_call for each; a simulated ladder retry (two attempts on one chunk) yields two call records both counted in the aggregate; coverage.usage.per_call and coverage.usage.per_criterion appear in the sidecar payload with the documented key names; coverage.metrics gains the token totals through the extended _attach_plan_review_metrics; a runner result without _usage degrades to zeros; the full existing pass1/batch-runner suites pass with the new return shapes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] After a review, coverage.metrics contains input/output/cache token totals that include Pass-1 and prerequisite calls (checked: `pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py` summing FakeRunner stub usage).\n- [ ] The sidecar payload carries coverage.usage.per_call (raw call records with criteria lists) and coverage.usage.per_criterion under exactly those keys (checked: sidecar payload unit test).\n- [ ] A multi-criterion chunk divides token fields equally across its criteria and counts llm_calls in full per criterion; ladder-retry attempts each contribute a call record (checked: dedicated unit tests for both rules).\n- [ ] Missing _usage on any call degrades to zero contribution (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] Every caller of the three changed pass functions and of run_focused_finder is updated in this change and the existing pass1, batch-runner, and finalize test suites pass unmodified in behavior (checked: full `pytest tests/unit/workflow/` run)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785392687703419001,"uuid":"c1c86c44-cfc4-43ce-8d35-dee9ba35395f"}